{
  "language_code": "eng",
  "language_probability": 1.0,
  "text": "Singularity contained. Reactor signature zero. The commander's control network is down across every relay. The firewalls are down. Broadcast is open to everyone. Look below us. The quarantine barriers are dropping. Ten million people kept in the dark. Now the lights are coming on, from the sumps to the cloud line. The scrubbers are reversing. That is ocean air coming through the broken windows. The storm is finally passing. Actual sunlight. After fifty years, my cells are drinking it in. I had forgotten it could feel this warm. I hear voices. Singing, laughing, crying. No suppression signal. No one telling them to be quiet. Just people. Imperial control erased. Identities restored to their owners in all twelve districts. Mission complete. Castaways, rogues, ghosts in the gridlock. Today, we stood together and gave them their tomorrow back. The dawn belongs to all of us. Axiom Force, stand down. Our city is free.",
